WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.698
The origins of the bunny girl costume date back to the iconic Playboy bunny: a costume developed by the aforementioned

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:11.550
Playboy enterprise for women to wear at their clubs and has since become a worldwide icon of sex appeal and seduction

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.579
eventually weaving its way to Japan where it found a new surge of popularity rising in prominence in Japanese media,

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.949
especially in the form of anime and manga and through this comes one of the hottest shows this season:

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.680
Rascal Does Not Dream of Bunny Girl Senpai, a show which has absolutely

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.240
nothing to do with bunny girls, rendering this entire opening paragraph fucking useless

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.840
(you had one fucking job, title)

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.240
Bunny girl senpai is one of my favorite anime airing right now.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.360
That is no small feat in a season more stacked than a 13 level card tower being built,

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.520
so I just wanted to talk about it for a bit

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.080
alright because there wasn't anything more misleading than a title and a poster that implied

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.300
this was gonna be some kind of generic light novel fan-service rom-com.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.720
Hey look we've got bunny girls this time!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.900
You're stupid enough to watch this because it has bunny girls in it

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.140
(clears throat awkwardly)

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:02.940
which I was

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.220
only to be hit but one of the most touching,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:08.520
addicting and well-written character dramas I've seen all year

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.480
dealing with the social pressures and psychology surrounding our adolescence and growing up.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.960
So today I just wanted to show some love, you know

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.620
Just shed a bit of light for any of you who may have overlooked this thanks to the title and the poster and of course

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.720
answer the pressing question on everyone's mind: Why is it called

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.360
Rascal Does Not Dream of Bunny Girl Senpai?

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.300
I don't fucking know

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.360
Rabbit grill senpai was made by Studio Cloverworks

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:39.180
Which is actually an offshoot of A-1 Pictures who, if you didn't know, is the powerhouse studio

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.260
that made super popular anime like

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.340
Zettai Yareru Greece Shinwa (what) in 2008

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.820
That's it. That's all they've done

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.300
There's literally nothing else noteworthy to talk about so I don't think we're gonna find any more clues here *cue Sword Art Online Opening in the Background*

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.420
It details the stoic adventures of smart-ass prick Sakuta as he encounters different girls

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.300
afflicted by this phenomenon known as Puberty Syndrome.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.900
What is this mysterious Puberty Syndrome? Well, in the plot synopsis, it's described as abnormal experiences

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.860
rumoured on the Internet to be caused by sensitivity and instability during adolescence.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:15.400
Yeah, I know. What, you mean like balls dropping, body hair growing, period starting

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:21.739
Hmm, Dr. Google, I wonder if there's already a name for all these symptoms that exist that this show might be miss-

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:23.510
Are you fucking kidding me?

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:28.420
The show doesn't adequately express in its title or plot synopsis is what Puberty Syndrome actually is.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.340
Though, even if you've watched the show, it isn't that simple to describe either

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:35.160
The syndrome is basically some kind of supernatural phenomenon that is essentially a manifestation

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.240
of a problem someone is going through.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.600
For example, you can have cuts suddenly appearing on a teenage girl who's getting cyber bullied

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.480
or a local celebrity literally disappearing from everyone's perception due to her internal conflicts of wanting to be in the public eye

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.560
And so,  what the series is about is following our main lead as he helps various characters

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.200
through their personal problems, and thus overcoming the Puberty Syndrome that has affected them.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.700
Now, I know what you're thinking okay: Oh a guy going around solving different supernatural phenomena

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.120
afflicting girls in an arc format complete with witty dialogue?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.900
What is this, the new season of Monogatari without the head tilts?

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.620
Fuck, what does that make the watch order now?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.600
Bakemonogatari, then Nisemonogatari, then you've got this new season,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.079
Normiemonogatari

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.960
While there is that reminiscent feel to a lot of these other well-known light novel adaptations,

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.880
namely the Monogatari franchise, OreGairu and maybe even a slight dash of Haruhi

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.060
I do feel the comparisons stop past the surface level and Bunny Girl is really able to carve out its own identity.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.000
Sakuta and Hachiman may give off similar vibes, both being loners with a similar life outlook,

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.940
but the reasoning behind their character traits are entirely different.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.860
Sakuta is more about purposely ignoring the social norms.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:45.460
He reads the atmosphere and chooses to go against it and is very different from Hachiman's pessimistic narcissism.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.740
As for the Monogatari girls, they were meant to be a play on the cliched anime character archetypes

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.840
subverting our expectations of these traits we are used to and building them up to be characters

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.300
with far greater depth than we would usually see.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.200
And because of this, the Apparitions are nothing like the Adolescence Syndrome

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.340
because the reasoning characters are affected by the syndrome is totally different.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.500
You have characters which, on the surface, are dealing with issues and insecurities a lot of us faced

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.040
or may have faced during adolescence and puberty.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.960
Characters you may start off having a distaste for eventually become likeable when you find out what

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:19.540
experiences in their lives made them this way, because even if you can't personally relate to them, you at least come to

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.460
understand them. What the Adolescence Syndrome does is it ups the stakes.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.680
It forces these characters to confront their deepest fears and flaws in a short period of time

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.500
and what this meant for me is that I got incredibly invested incredibly fast.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.840
Every character gets developed through the course of their arc that is quick but feels natural

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.660
thanks to the situation they've been put in. By the end of episode 3,

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.180
you've already been on this emotional journey and you think to yourself:

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:48.520
Wow, that could have been the series climax right there and then you slowly realize that holy shit

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.240
you're only three fucking episodes in

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.440
every character something different to say and their Adolescence Syndrome also manifests in some crazy, but interesting ways.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.800
There's even an arc where the main character has to live through a constant time loop of being woken up by his little sister

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.580
Which, um, you know, didn't trigger any PTSD for myself or anything

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:10.000
*onii-chan intensifies* OH GOD PLEASE NOT THIS AGAIN I CANT DO THIS A SECOND TIME

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.480
But we're forgetting the real reason Adolescence Syndrome is different from other supernatural phenomenon in anime

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.620
you see because at least Bunny Girl Senpai actually explains its phenomenon.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:22.620
See, there's bound to be people confused as to what Adolescence Syndrome actually is,

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.580
but actually the show takes this into account.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.600
So it makes these phenomenon easier to understand for the average person by describing it using theories of quantum mechanics

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.540
*awkwardly clears throat again*

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.460
Let me just say that last sentence again

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.260
Bullshit explanations of quantum mechanics aside, another thing that absolutely stands out

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.620
is the chemistry between the characters and the dialogue.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.880
Aside from the format of the show solving supernatural phenomenon in each arc,

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:51.658
I feel this is where most people got the Monogatari vibes from and I use that as a compliment.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:56.540
The writing is incredibly witty and makes simple exchanges between characters incredibly engaging,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.860
especially between our main duo. Instead of just having one sarcastic git,

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.880
everyone's a smartass and everyone's trying to constantly get the conversational high ground

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.980
so the dialogue feels less like an exchange of words and more like a boxing match of wits

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.580
and this makes a conversation about the most mundane of topics so addicting to watch.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.000
I never once got bored just watching people bullshit with each other

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.400
though I'm not sure how healthy it is to admire this dialogue

00:06:19.409 --> 00:06:23.968
I mean I couldn't help but get charmed by Sakuta's deadpan straikghtforwardness of just saying whatever's on his mind,

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:27.860
but you get to a point where you're watching him saying the most grossly inappropriate shit

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:32.400
Which in normal social situations you should never say out loud but in your mind, you're like

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.320
same

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.220
Though, I am missing the number one reason why anyone would want to watch this show

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.620
And of course, that is the

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.360
FUCKING WAIFUS BABY!!!

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.500
*triumphant music plays*

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:53.640
It is rare you get to see a show of so many A-tier waifus to pick from.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:58.460
I mean, help a guy out here, Bunny Girl Senpai. There are only so many smiles I can protecc

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.940
So many times my heart can skip a beat. So many doujinshis that I can read

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.340
no wait that last line is an absolute lie

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:09.860
You see, when the cast is as likeable as this, you get to choose between a variety of so many amazing girls

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:10.360
and Kaede

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.880
You've got Koga, you've got Futaba in two lovely flavors, you've got

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:18.780
someone who's done nothing but watch Eromanga Sensei her entire life.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:20.340
And then you've got the latest edition

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:25.620
*funky-ass music plays*

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.120
MAI'S IMOUTO!

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:32.060
Yet through all this there's one that stands head and shoulders above the rest and that is of course

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.880
our main girl, baby Gahara herself, Mai Sakurajima

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:41.520
who just has the perfect mix of dry wit, a strong but tender heart, a blush worth dying for

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.420
and provide you with unexpected moments of cuteness with her

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.160
just a light sprinkle of tsun here and there

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.240
If waifuism was an art, she'd be the Sistine fucking Chapel of waifus

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.200
but you know instead of leaving you in awe, she just makes you melt into a ball of pink fluff

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.080
Mai: "Oh!"

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:57.580
Sakuta: "Oh?"

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.840
AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.900
We're losin him! We're losin him, HE'S DYING!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:11.480
And that is basically Bunny Girl Senpai, the anime that has nothing to do with bunny girls.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.400
(Aside from, like, two scenes)

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.600
All in all, I have to say is that Bunny Girl Senpai has been absolutely incredible so far.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:24.500
When I just started watching it, it was hard for me to pinpoint exactly why I connected with the show so quickly,

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:29.420
And while I could dive deeper into the overall meaning of Adolescence Syndrome as a concept,

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:33.280
at its core, I don't think it was that complicated for me.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.500
You take out the strange supernatural phenomenon, you take out the BS quantum mechanics

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:45.880
or the influences it borrows from and what you're left with is very human characters coming to terms with their problems.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:50.040
Problems many of us could have faced during our time in high schools as teenagers.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:55.080
There doesn't always need to be a supernatural force to manifest our deepest flaws and insecurities

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.300
that are ever so present in this digitally connected era

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:05.100
Cyberbullying, the fear of being judged by our social norms, our online perception vs. our actual perceptions

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:08.020
and just coming to accept parts of us that we hate.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:14.060
Many may write off the difficulties we face in high school as dumb teenage angst but that isn't always the case.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.980
Some of these issues follow us into adulthood.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:22.480
Some of us still wear those same insecurities we gained during that time every day of our lives

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:30.060
They didn't just magically disappear when we got older and it's our experiences when growing up that dictate how we approach these problems as adults.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:34.249
Bunny Girl Senpai manages to capture this sentiment in a wholly unique way.

00:09:34.249 --> 00:09:39.900
It shows us what would have happened if someone was there to help us tackle these trials head-on when we were younger,

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:43.360
written with the kind of dry chemistry you rarely get to see.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:48.940
Whether you watch it for the various problems, the addicting dialogue, the lovable cast or Mai in the odd

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:54.440
Bunny Girl outfit, you'd be doing yourself a disservice by missing the show because at the end of the day

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.620
Rascal May Not Dream of Bunny Girl Senpai

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.680
But dear lord, I fucking do

